200.description:
Returns the add account URL widget to be invoked by the client

Set the optional **source** field to **MX** to connect a bank via MX (for banks Finicity does not support); omit it (or use FINICITY) for the default Finicity flow. When **source=MX**, widgetUrl is an MX Connect URL (moneydesktop.com) loaded with the MX Connect widget instead of the Finicity SDK below; omit institutionId to let the user search for their bank in the widget.

When the call succeed, returning code 200, grab the content of widgetUrl and make a call to this url. See below:

Example of returning JSON:
{
  "status": "OK",
  "widgetUrl": "https://connect.finicity.com?analytics=google%3AUA-123456789-1&customerId=53829905&partnerId=2445582741601&redirectUri=https%3A%2F%2Fce5d9f86.ngrok.io%2Fapi%2Fpublic%2Fredirect-handler&signature=4837879cbdab90530c5191bec7209719cbb25657d38b6d6e862f809d44aaf661&timestamp=1589996840006&ttl=1590004040006&type=aggregation&webhook=https%3A%2F%2Fce5d9f86.ngrok.io%2Fapi%2Fpublic%2Fwebhook-handler&webhookContentType=application%2Fjson"
}

** Include the below script on your page ** 
	<script&nbsp;src="https://connect.finicity.com/assets/sdk/finicity-connect.min.js"></script>

** Make this call to trigger the widget ** 
			window['finicityConnect']['connectIFrame']('**ADD THE CONTENT OF widgetUrl HERE**', {
                            success: () => {
                                console.log('success');
                            },
                            cancel : () => {
                                console.log('cancel');
                            },
                            error  : () => {
                                console.log('error');
                            },
                            loaded : () => {
                                console.log('loaded');
                            }
                        });
